 "news": {
  "date": "2026-11-05",
  "asof": "2026-11-06 06:49 UTC",
  "headline": "The worst day since April 2025 \u2014 chips crash on data-centre fears, and the Nasdaq enters a correction",
  "standfirst": "The S&P fell 4.36%, the Nasdaq 5.52% and the Russell 4.45%, their worst day since April 2025, as investors priced slower data-centre growth under a Democratic Congress. Technology fell 8%, with AMD down 17.26% and Nvidia 9.26%, and the VIX jumped to 28.18. The two-year yield fell about 12bp on soft labour costs and December hike odds dropped to about two-thirds, while WTI rose 2.72% to $90.52. The book is flat; Q4 is +34.64 realised, heat 0R.",
  "themes": [
   {
    "kicker": "What's next",
    "right": "Friday: payrolls",
    "title": "Payrolls on the morning after a crash",
    "items": [
     {
